Subject: [ESP-60 DIAGNOSTIC] i2c_master: reset command FSM before every transaction

ESP-60-M5STACKCHAN-NFC diagnostic patch. NOT for upstream/production as-is.

Root-cause hypothesis (see ticket design-doc/05): the ESP-IDF 5.5.4 new I2C
master driver resets the I2C command FSM only REACTIVELY (when the previous
transaction left status==TIMEOUT or the bus reads busy). M5GFX's direct
backend resets the FSM on EVERY transaction (common.cpp:2000,
dev->ctr.fsm_rst = 1). Under high-frequency ST25R3916 IRQ polling the
inherited FSM state occasionally produces a marginal START/address that
the slave NACKs, surfacing as ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE (I2C_EVENT_NACK,
confirmed via driver DEBUG; zero timeouts).

This patch makes the reset in s_i2c_transaction_start() UNCONDITIONAL,
mirroring M5GFX, using clear_bus=false (the cheap fsm_rst bit toggle, not
the heavier bus-clear+reinit recovery path) so the per-transaction cost
stays minimal and the comparison is fair.

Decision rule (design-doc/05 section 7.2):
  - NACK rate -> ~0   : root cause confirmed; implement preventive reset as a
                        local ST25R3916 backend (not an IDF fork).
  - unchanged (~1%)   : controller-state cleanliness is wrong; pivot to
                        SDA/SCL capture to locate the NACK byte stage.

Base: ESP-IDF v5.5.4 commit 73550728
File: components/esp_driver_i2c/i2c_master.c
